# Backend (NestJS modular monolith)

## Module layout

```text
modules/<domain>/
  *.module.ts · controllers/ · services/ · dto/ · (guards/strategies as needed)
common/ · config/ · prisma/
```

Bounded contexts stay extractable later (see `docs/architecture/backend-architecture.md`).

## Controllers vs services

- Controllers: receive → validate DTO → call service → return.
- Business logic in services/domain — never 100-line controller methods.
- No cross-module writes to another module’s tables; use facades/events.

## DTOs & validation

- Every external input has a DTO + validation (body/query/params/files).
- Never trust the client.

## API shape

- Versioned REST `/v1/...`; nouns not verbs (`GET /users`, not `/getAllUsers`).
- Correct HTTP status codes (not 200 for everything).
- Consistent envelopes:

```json
{ "success": true, "data": {}, "message": "..." }
{ "success": true, "data": [], "meta": { "page": 1, "limit": 20, "total": 100, "totalPages": 5 } }
{ "success": false, "message": "...", "code": "USER_NOT_FOUND" }
```

- Never expose stack traces, SQL, or secrets to clients.

## AuthZ

- Authentication ≠ authorization; enforce both **server-side**.
- Prefer `@Roles()` / policies / scope guards (State/Local territory).
- Frontend checks are UX only.

## Errors & logging

- No empty `catch`. Central filters; structured logs with request/user context.
- Never log passwords, tokens, or secrets. Prefer logger over `console.log` in prod paths.

## Config

- Env vars only; validate at startup; fail fast if critical config missing.
